---
source: crates/nash-ast/src/head.rs
description: "Coverage of a wanted predicate whose arguments are rigid variables. Big covers Big; Little covers Const and Term. One budget pays for subject discovery, the cells, and every selection."
---
Big and Little impls, given at 'a
  'a Big selects big; 'a Const selects little; 'a Term selects little
only a Big impl, given at 'a
  no impl for the cell 'a Const
Big and Little impls, no given
  needs the trait at 'a
only a Big impl, no given (the limit comes first)
  needs the trait at 'a
Big and Little impls, the argument can still change
  not applicable
pair impls, given at 'a and 'b
  'a Big, 'b Big selects first big; 'a Big, 'b Const selects first big; 'a Big, 'b Term selects first big; 'a Const, 'b Big selects first little, second big; 'a Const, 'b Const selects both little; 'a Const, 'b Term selects both little; 'a Term, 'b Big selects first little, second big; 'a Term, 'b Const selects both little; 'a Term, 'b Term selects both little
pair impls, given at 'a only
  needs the trait at 'b
pair impls, one step less than the whole search
  work limit
